### Part 1: Creating Encryption and Decryption Keys

The RSA algorithm involves the following steps to generate keys:
1. Choose two large prime numbers \( p \) and \( q \).
2. Compute \( n = p \times q \).
3. Compute the totient \( \phi(n) = (p-1) \times (q-1) \).
4. Choose an integer \( e \) such that \( 1 < e < \phi(n) \) and \( e \) is coprime with \( \phi(n) \).
5. Compute \( d \) such that \( d \times e \equiv 1 \mod \phi(n) \).

